## Reproduce

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt
.venv/bin/python scripts/run_all.py    # every table, chart, metrics.json, and this README
.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q          # unit tests, including README / IC numbers vs metrics.json
```

The random seed is {{inputs.robustness.seed}} everywhere. All assumptions live in `config/`.

## Dashboard

An interactive Plotly Dash app in `dashboard/` reuses the model code in `src/alm` and the saved results in `outputs/`. The Optimizer page re-solves the LP live for a chosen capital budget, constraint switches and CLO factor regime. The other pages (rate risk, cash flows, capital, stress tests, robustness, methodology) show portfolios A, B and C from the saved holdings and outputs, recomputed at startup with the same code as `scripts/run_all.py` where a table is not saved.

Live demo: https://insurance-alm-model-portfolio-production.up.railway.app

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m dashboard.app      # local development server, port 8050 (or $PORT)
```

- Production, the start command in `railway.json`: `gunicorn dashboard.app:server --bind 0.0.0.0:$PORT --workers 1 --threads 4 --timeout 120` <!-- static -->
- Railway installs `requirements.txt` with the Python version in `.python-version`. The healthcheck path `/health` returns 503 until the model cache is built at startup, then 200.
- After changing `config/`, rerun `scripts/run_all.py` so the saved results the dashboard reads stay in sync.

## Limitations

- Market data, spreads, PDs, recoveries, CPRs and the liability block are synthetic.
- Liability cash flows do not respond to rates (no dynamic lapse), which understates rate risk. The Agency MBS prepayment S-curve is illustrative, not fitted to data.
- **The liability block is closed and terminates at year {{phase2.liability_truncation.horizon_years}}.**
  - The same benefit shape run to year {{phase2.liability_truncation.extended_horizon}} (flat curve beyond 30Y) would have {{phase2.liability_truncation.pv_share_beyond_horizon|.1%}} of its PV after year {{phase2.liability_truncation.horizon_years}}.
  - The reserve V_t only runs to year {{phase2.liability_truncation.horizon_years}}, so surrenders in the last ten years are {{phase2.liability_truncation.late_surrender_ratio|.0%}} of what an open-ended block would pay.
- The swap overlay result depends on a zero swap spread, no collateral or margin, and a carry of {{phase6.overlay.carry_bp|+.0f}}bp a year.
- Annual time steps; credit losses use a bond-level PD; designations for structured bonds are illustrative.
- C-1 charge = value × factor (book-value proxy under stress). There is no bond size factor, tax, covariance or RBC ratio. Derivatives carry no modeled capital.
- The LP is linear and lands on corner solutions; see the robustness simulation.

